      "claim": "In rats fed a blackberry anthocyanin-enriched diet, cyanidin-3-O-glucoside was the predominant anthocyanin in brain homogenate and its brain content exceeded plasma, directly demonstrating brain access of a glycosylated polyphenol.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C13"],
      "claim": "Cyanidin-3-O-glucoside was detected in human brain vascular endothelium and brain tissue, indicating transfer across the highly selective human blood-brain barrier.",
